     "text": "The name of this surah is taken from its first verse \"idha ja'aka al-munafiqun\". This surah was revealed about the hypocrites who from time to time became a cause of hurt to the Holy Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), insulted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and waited for misfortunes to befall the noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them). In this surah their double-faced character and evil qualities are mentioned, so the name of the surah has been kept Surah al-Munafiqun.\nThis surah is Madani. According to most commentators it was revealed in 5 AH or 6 AH after the battle of Banu al-Mustaliq. On the return from the battle of Banu al-Mustaliq, at the place of Muraysi', a quarrel arose between a Muhajir and an Ansari over filling water at a watering place, and 'Abdullah ibn Ubayy, the chief of the hypocrites, said harsh things against the Holy Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them). A young Companion, Sayyiduna Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him), informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of this. On being questioned, the chief of the hypocrites 'Abdullah ibn Ubayy swore false oaths; then this surah was revealed.",
