   "content": "<p>Question 3: Give detailed answers to the following questions:</p><p>(1a) يَقُولُونَ لَئِن رَّجَعْنَآ إِلَى ٱلْمَدِينَةِ لَيُخْرِجَنَّ ٱلْأَعَزُّ مِنْهَا ٱلْأَذَلَّ ۚ وَلِلَّهِ ٱلْعِزَّةُ وَلِرَسُولِهِۦ وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱلْمُنَٰفِقِينَ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ — Write the translation of the verse.</p><p>(1b) — Write an introduction to Surah al-Munafiqun.</p><p>(2a) وَلَن يُؤَخِّرَ ٱللَّهُ نَفْسًا إِذَا جَآءَ أَجَلُهَا ۚ وَٱللَّهُ خَبِيرٌۢ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ — Write the translation of the verse.</p><p>(2b) — Write some basic themes of Surah al-Munafiqun.</p><p>(3a) يَوْمَ يَجْمَعُكُمْ لِيَوْمِ ٱلْجَمْعِ ۖ ذَٰلِكَ يَوْمُ ٱلتَّغَابُنِ ۗ وَمَن يُؤْمِنۢ بِٱللَّهِ وَيَعْمَلْ صَٰلِحًۭا يُكَفِّرْ عَنْهُ سَيِّـَٔاتِهِۦ وَيُدْخِلْهُ جَنَّٰتٍۢ تَجْرِى مِن تَحْتِهَا ٱلْأَنْهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَآ أَبَدًۭا ۚ ذَٰلِكَ ٱلْفَوْزُ ٱلْعَظِيمُ — Write the translation of the verse.</p><p>(3b) — Write an introduction to Surah al-Taghabun.</p><p>(4a) يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓا۟ إِنَّ مِنْ أَزْوَٰجِكُمْ وَأَوْلَٰدِكُمْ عَدُوًّۭا لَّكُمْ فَٱحْذَرُوهُمْ ۚ وَإِن تَعْفُوا۟ وَتَصْفَحُوا۟ وَتَغْفِرُوا۟ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٌۭ رَّحِيمٌ — Write the translation of the verse.</p><p>(4b) — Write some basic themes of Surah al-Taghabun.</p><p>Activities for students</p><p>Collect information about the signs of hypocrisy, the character of the hypocrites of Madinah and their end, and discuss it.</p><p>Learn from your teachers the details of the matters declared beneficial for the people of faith in verses 14 to 18 of Surah al-Taghabun.</p><p>Collect the attributes of Allah Almighty stated in Surah al-Taghabun and reflect on their meanings.</p><p>Guidance for teachers</p><p>Make the students aware of the importance and virtues of spending in the way of Allah in the light of the Qur&#x27;an and Sunnah.</p><p>What should be the attitude of a believer in afflictions? Explain by giving some example from the Qur&#x27;an Majid, the blessed hadiths and the Prophetic Sirah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).</p>",
