   "content": "<p>Lesson 24 — Surah al-Talaq and Surah al-Tahrim</p><p>Surah al-Talaq (verses 1 to 12)</p><p>Reason for the name and introduction</p><p>The name of this surah is taken from its first verse &quot;ya ayyuha al-nabiyyu idha tallaqtumu al-nisa&#x27;a fa-tallaquhunna li-&#x27;iddatihinna&quot;. The literal meaning of talaq is release, freedom, getting free. In Shari&#x27;ah terminology it is to end the marriage bond established between husband and wife by means of specific words. In case of domestic disputes this step sometimes becomes unavoidable, although this is a disliked act in the sight of Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The name of this surah is &quot;Surah al-Talaq&quot; because in it commands concerning divorce and the matters arising after it have been stated. Sayyiduna &#x27;Abdullah ibn Mas&#x27;ud (may Allah be pleased with him) also called this surah &quot;al-Nisa&#x27; al-Qusra&quot; (the shorter al-Nisa&#x27;). (Sahih Bukhari, 4532) The fourth surah of the Qur&#x27;an-e-Majid, &quot;al-Nisa&#x27; al-Tula&quot;, is a long surah containing commands concerning women. This surah is comparatively short; in it too commands concerning women have been stated, so its name has also been kept &quot;al-Nisa&#x27; al-Qusra&quot;.\nSurah al-Talaq was revealed in Madinah Munawwarah. It is the saying of Sayyiduna &#x27;Abdullah ibn Mas&#x27;ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that Surah al-Talaq was revealed after those verses of Surah al-Baqarah in which the commands of divorce were given for the first time. (Sahih Bukhari, 4532) The necessary issues of divorce had been stated in Surah al-Baqarah. In this surah some remaining basic issues among those same issues are being set out so that the statement of these issues may be completed.</p><p>Central theme</p><p>The etiquette and commands of family life</p><p>Basic themes</p><p>1. The commands of divorce and the command to adopt piety in carrying them out</p><p>2. A statement of the waiting period (iddah) of different women</p><p>3. The commands of residence and maintenance for a divorced woman</p><p>4. Warning to the deniers of the truth of the end of earlier nations, and a lesson to be learnt</p><p>5. The instruction to strengthen one&#x27;s connection with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Qur&#x27;an Majid</p><p>6. A statement of the attributes of knowledge and power of Allah Almighty</p>",
